    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n28152" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Massŭrĭus</span></b>  (<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Măsŭrĭus</span></b> )
		Sabinus, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>a celebrated jurist in the time of the emperor
				Tiberius</i>, <i><span class="en">Dig. 1, 2, 2 <i>fin.</i></span></i>; <i><span class="en">Gell. 3, 16 <i>fin.</i></span></i>; <i><span class="en">5, 19
				al.</span></i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Masuri rubrica vetavit,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Pers.
					5, 90</span></i>
			. —Hence, <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Masŭrĭānus</span></b> , a,
			um, <i>adj., of</i> or <i>pertaining to Massurius</i>: deliramenta, M. Aurel. ap. <i><span class="en">Front. Ep. ad Caes. 2, 9</span></i> Mai.</div>
